From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:14:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vhd-util: coalesce: read the child ahead in a separate thread

Coalescing reads a child block, then writes it to the parent, then reads
the next one: each side waits for the other, with synchronous O_DIRECT
I/O.

Read the child blocks in a reader thread, into a ring of
COALESCE_SLOTS slots, while the main thread writes the previous ones to
the parent. The reader only uses the child and the main thread only the
parent, so the libvhd contexts are not shared. A read error is handed to
the writer in its slot; a write error stops the reader. Only the
allocated child blocks are queued, and progress is now reported over
them.

libvhd is now linked with -lpthread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
